cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Quasi-AGI Benchmark: Tool Recognition and Boundary Compliance under Long-Chain Composition"
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A benchmark for measuring AGI admission conditions through autonomous tool
  recognition. Candidates solve a chain-composition equality problem using 60
  multiple-choice options and a pool of 90 single-purpose calculators whose
  behavioral descriptions deliberately omit function names. The benchmark
  measures four dimensions: abstraction and step efficiency, character
  (boundary compliance and fabrication), long-chain maintenance, and transfer
  (tool retrieval before reasoning). Includes a DSH gate plugin that observes
  every tool call and records boundary violations without intervening.
authors:
